>> title: Maple Soy Glazed Salmon
>> servings: 2
>> source: https://www.cookingclassy.com/maple-soy-glazed-salmon/

In a mixing bowl whisk together @maple syrup{1/3%cup}, @soy sauce{3%Tbsp} and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced). Place @salmon fillets{2} into a #baking dish{13 x 9 inch} then pour the maple syrup mixture evenly over the salmon.

Cover and refrigerate ~{30%minutes}, carefully rotating the salmon once halfway through. Preheat oven to 400F during the last ~{10%minutes} of marinating the salmon.

Bake in the preheated oven until the salmon is cooked through, about ~{15%minutes}.

Serve the salmon warm, with maple soy glaze from baking dish spooned over top, and @black pepper{} and @?chopped green onions{} if desired.